  CardStory: "The first thing Spades2 notices is that everyone is becoming very good
    at remembering things. Makes sense, he supposes. The Order is built on memory.\r\n\r\nNames
    and ranks, procedures and passwords. The number of bolts in the western gate.
    18. The exact weight of every blade in the armory. 74.623 kilograms. Which corridors
    flood when the generators fail. But no longer, because they don\u2019t fail anymore.
    Which recruits have brothers, or sisters, or no family at all. But that is just
    professional courtesy, isn\u2019t it? And respect.\r\n\r\n\u201CI remember my
    comrades because one day I may have to recognise them in the dark. I remember
    the dead, because someone must.\u201D And Spades2 remembers himself, because
    nobody else can do it for me.\r\n\r\nThat is what Sergeant Spades6 tells Spades2.
    Always has. Has she? Yes, she has.\r\n\r\nNo one says otherwise."
